---
import Layout from '../layouts/BlogPost.astro';
---

<Layout
	title="About Chronically Us"
	description="Stories, Strength, and Support for Life with Chronic Illness."
	pubDate={new Date()}
	heroImage="/blog-placeholder-3.jpg"
>
	<h2>Welcome to Chronically Us</h2>

	<p>
		Hi, I'm Julia, and I created Chronically Us as a place where people living
		with chronic illnesses can share their experiences, connect with others,
		and find comfort in knowing they are not alone.
	</p>

	<p>
		Living with a chronic condition can be challenging in ways that are often
		invisible to others. Some days bring victories, some days bring setbacks,
		and many days involve navigating a reality that others may not fully
		understand.
	</p>

	<p>
		This site was created to make space for those stories. Whether you're newly
		diagnosed, have been managing symptoms for years, support a loved one with
		a chronic illness, or simply want to learn from others, you're welcome
		here.
	</p>

	<h2>Our Mission</h2>

	<p>
		Chronically Us exists to create a compassionate and supportive community
		where people can share experiences, express frustrations, celebrate
		progress, and learn from one another.
	</p>

	<p>
		Through personal stories, community prompts, and honest conversations, we
		hope to remind people that every experience matters and every voice
		deserves to be heard.
	</p>

	<h2>What You'll Find Here</h2>

	<ul>
		<li>Personal stories and lived experiences</li>
		<li>Community discussion prompts</li>
		<li>Encouragement and support</li>
		<li>Resources and shared perspectives</li>
		<li>A welcoming environment built on empathy and respect</li>
	</ul>

	<h2>A Quick Note</h2>

	<p>
		The content shared on Chronically Us reflects personal experiences and
		community perspectives. It is not intended to replace professional medical
		advice, diagnosis, or treatment.
	</p>

	<p>
		Most importantly, we want this to be a place where people feel seen,
		understood, and supported.
	</p>

	<blockquote>
		You are more than your diagnosis. Your story matters.
	</blockquote>
</Layout>

